tween dirichlet and Neumann eigenvalues"],"prefix":"10.1007","volume":"94","author":[{"given":"Howard A.","family":"Levine","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Hans F.","family":"Weinberger","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"297","reference":[{"key":"CR1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","unstructured":"P. Aviles, Symmetry theorems related to Pompeiu's problem. American J. of Math. (in press).","DOI":"10.2307\/2374594"},{"key":"CR2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","DOI":"10.1007\/978-3-642-47404-0","volume-title":"Theorie der Konvexen K\u00f6rper","author":"T. Bonessen","year":"1934","unstructured":"T. Bonessen & W. Fenchel, Theorie der Konvexen K\u00f6rper. Springer, Berlin, 1934, Chelsea, New York, 1948."},{"key":"CR3","volume-title":"Methods of Mathematical Physics, vol. I","author":"R. Courant","year":"1962","unstructured":"R. Courant & D. Hilbert, Methods of Mathematical Physics, vol. I, Interscience, New York (1962)."},{"key":"CR4","volume-title":"Inequalities","author":"G. H. Hardy","year":"1952","unstructured":"G. H. Hardy, J. E. Littlewood, & G. Polya, Inequalities, 2nd ed., Cambridge U. Press, London, 1952.","edition":"2nd ed."},{"key":"CR5","first-page":"517","volume":"4","author":"L. E. Payne","year":"1955","unstructured":"L. E. Payne, Inequalities for eigenvalues of plates and membranes, J. Rational Mech. Anal. 4 (1955), 517?529.","journal-title":"J. Rational Mech. Anal."},{"key":"CR6","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"55","DOI":"10.1002\/sapm195231155","volume":"31","author":"G. Polya","year":"1952","unstructured":"G. Polya, Remarks on the foregoing paper, J. of Math, and Phys. 31 (1952), 55?57.","journal-title":"J. of Math, and Phys."},{"key":"CR7","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","DOI":"10.1007\/978-1-4612-5282-5","volume-title":"Maximum Principles in Differential Equations","author":"M. H. Protter","year":"1984","unstructured":"M. H. Protter & H. F. Weinberger, Maximum Principles in Differential Equations. Prentice Hall, Englewood Cliffs, 1967, Springer, New York, 1984."},{"key":"CR8","volume-title":"C.B.M.S. Regional Conf. Ser. # 15","author":"H. F. Weinberger","year":"1974","unstructured":"H. F. Weinberger, Variational Methods for Eigenvalue Approximation, C.B.M.S. Regional Conf. Ser. # 15, S.I.A.M., Philadelphia, 1974."}],"container-title":["Archive for Rational Mechanics and Analysis"],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"http:\/\/link.springer.com\/content\/pdf\/10.1007\/BF00279862.pdf","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"http:\/\/link.springer.com\/article\/10.1007\/BF00279862\/fulltext.html","content-type":"text\/html","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"http:\/\/link.springer.com\/content\/pdf\/10.1007\/BF00279862","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2019,4,3]],"date-time":"2019-04-03T18:27:38Z","timestamp":1554316058000},"score":26.800838,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"http:\/\/link.springer.com\/10.1007\/BF00279862"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[1986]]},"references-count":8,"journal-issue":{"issue":"3","published-print":{"date-parts":[[1986]]}},"alternative-id":["BF00279862"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1007\/bf00279862","ISSN":["0003-9527","1432-0673"],"issn-type":[{"value":"0003-9527","type":"print"},{"value":"1432-0673","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[1986]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2025,7,30]],"date-time":"2025-07-30T16:43:22Z","timestamp":1753893802604,"version":"3.41.2"},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"The Electronic Journal of Combinatorics","issue":"1","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Electron. J. Combin."],"abstract":"<jats:p>Let $G$ be a simple connected graph and $\\mu_1(G) \\geq \\mu_2(G) \\geq \\cdots \\geq \\mu_n(G)$ be the Laplacian eigenvalues of $G$. Let $\\overline{G}$ be the complement of $G$. Einollahzadeh et al.[J. Combin. Theory Ser. B, 151(2021), 235\u2013249] proved that $\\mu_{n-1}(G)+\\mu_{n-1}(\\overline{G})\\geq 1$. Grij\u00f2 et al. [Discrete Appl. Math., 267(2019), 176\u2013183] conjectured that $\\mu_{n-2}(G)+\\mu_{n-2}(\\overline{G})\\geq 2$ for any graph and proved it to be true for some graphs. In this paper, we prove $\\mu_{n-2}(G)+\\mu_{n-2}(\\overline{G})\\geq 2$ is true for some new graphs. Furthermore, we propose a more general conjecture that $\\mu_k(G)+\\mu_k(\\overline{G})\\geq n-k$ holds for any graph $G$, with equality if and only if $G$ or $\\overline{G}$ is isomorphic to $K_{n-k}\\vee H$, where $H$ is a disconnected graph on $k$ vertices and has at least $n-k+1$ connected components. And we prove that it is true for $k\\leq \\frac{n+1}{2}$, for unicyclic graphs, bicyclic graphs, threshold graphs, bipartite graphs, regular graphs, complete multipartite graphs and c-cyclic graphs when $n\\geq 2c+8$.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.37236\/12008","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,2,9]],"date-time":"2024-02-09T15:45:34Z","timestamp":1707493534000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Nordhaus-Gaddum Type Inequalities for the $k$th Largest Laplacian Eigenvalues"],"prefix":"10.37236","volume":"31","author":[{"given":"Wen-Jun","family":"Li","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Ji-Ming","family":"Guo","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"23455","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2024,2,9]]},"container-title":["The Electronic Journal of Combinatorics"],"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/www.combinatorics.org\/ojs\/index.php\/eljc\/article\/download\/v31i1p31\/pdf","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/www.combinatorics.org\/ojs\/index.php\/eljc\/article\/download\/v31i1p31\/pdf","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2024,2,9]],"date-time":"2024-02-09T15:45:35Z","timestamp":1707493535000},"score":26.796864,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.combinatorics.org\/ojs\/index.php\/eljc\/article\/view\/v31i1p31"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024,2,9]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"1","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2024,1,12]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.37236\/12008","ISSN":["1077-8926"],"issn-type":[{"type":"electronic","value":"1077-8926"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2024,2,9]]},"article-number":"P1.31"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2022,3,30]],"date-time":"2022-03-30T21:15:15Z","timestamp":1648674915272},"reference-count":0,"publisher":"University of Wyoming Libraries","content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["ELA"],"DOI":"10.13001\/1081-3810.1647","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2015,9,15]],"date-time":"2015-09-15T07:23:04Z","timestamp":1442301784000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Upper bounds for the largest eigenvalues of a bipartite graph"],"prefix":"10.13001","volume":"26","author":[{"given":"Jorma","family":"Merikoski","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Ravinder","family":"Kumar","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Ram","family":"Rajput","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"5168","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2013,1,1]]},"container-title":["The Electronic Journal of Linear Algebra"],"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/journals.uwyo.edu\/index.php\/ela\/article\/download\/1229\/1229","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL